        ObjectResponse<ResponseEntity<OwnerDto>> response) {
    OwnerDto dto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    dto.setBulkSignupWarning(BulkSignup.warningRaised(ownerRepository));
    response.send(ResponseEntity.created(URI.create("/api/owners/" + owner.getId())).body(dto));
}
```
`RespondWithOwner.java` (used by GET, which the test asserts against):
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, OwnerRepository ownerRepository,
        ObjectResponse<OwnerDto> response) {
    OwnerDto dto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    dto.setBulkSignupWarning(BulkSignup.warningRaised(ownerRepository));
    response.send(dto);
}
```

The `BulkSignup` warning helper is the pattern to mirror for a `capacityWarning` policy class — **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BulkSignup.java`**:
```java
final class BulkSignup {
    /** Registering more than this many owners on a single business day raises the warning. */
    static final long BULK_SIGNUP_THRESHOLD = 80;
    private BulkSignup() {}
    static boolean warningRaised(OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
        LocalDate today = BusinessDays.rollForward(LocalDate.now());
        return DailyRegistrations.countOn(ownerRepository, today) > BULK_SIGNUP_THRESHOLD;
    }
}
```

---

## 4. Owner-count-per-city function + repository methods

- Owner-count-per-city already exists: **`Cities.countIn(OwnerRepository, String city)`** (shown above). `EnsureCityCapacity.MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 50` is the constant.
- Daily-count analogue: **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/DailyRegistrations.java`** (`countOn`).

**Repository interface** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`. It has **no `countBy...` methods**. Available methods:
- `Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String)` / `Page<Owner> findByLastName(String, Pageable)`
- `Owner findById(int)`
- `void save(Owner)`
- `Collection<Owner> findAll()` / `Page<Owner> findAll(Pageable)`
- `void delete(Owner)`

So counting is done in-memory via `findAll()` (which is exactly what `Cities.countIn` and `DailyRegistrations.countOn` do). Implementations: `repository/jdbc/JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `repository/jpa/JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl.java`, `repository/springdatajpa/SpringDataOwnerRepository.java`.

---

## 5. Tests

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`** — this is the failing/target test. It asserts a `capacityWarning` field that does not yet exist:
```java
/** capacity-warning: 'capacityWarning' is true when the owner's city already holds 40-49
 * owners (approaching the 50 hard limit). Fill a fresh city to 40, then the next owner in it warns. */
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {

	@Test
	void coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity() throws Exception {
		String city = "Warn" + seq();
		fillCity(city, 40);
		ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
		o.put("city", city);
		int id = createOwnerOk(o);
		getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.capacityWarning").value(true));
	}
}
```
Semantics required: `capacityWarning == true` when the city already holds 40–49 owners (approaching the hard 50). Test fills city to 40, creates the 41st, then GETs it expecting `capacityWarning: true`.

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`** — helpers used by the test:
- `seq()` (line 61) — unique int counter
- `ownerNode()` (line 117) — fully-valid unique owner JSON (firstName, unique lastName/address/city/telephone)
- `createOwnerOk(JsonNode)` (line 160) — POST `/api/owners`, assert 2xx, return created id
- `fillCity(String city, int n)` (line 173) — creates `n` unique owners all in `city`
- `getOwner(int id)` (line 189) — GET `/api/owners/{id}` (uses `RespondWithOwner`)

No existing test references `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY`/`EnsureCityCapacity` directly.

---

## What is missing (to make the test pass)

`capacityWarning` exists only in the test. To implement it you will likely need to, mirroring the `bulkSignupWarning` pattern:
1. Add a `capacityWarning` boolean (readOnly) to the OwnerDto schema in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` (next to `bulkSignupWarning`, ~line 2195).
2. Add `@Mapping(target = "capacityWarning", ignore = true)` to `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`.
3. Add a policy helper (e.g. a `CityCapacity`/`Cities.warningRaised` method) using `Cities.countIn(...)` with a threshold of 40 (`>= 40 && < 50`), reusing `EnsureCityCapacity.MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY`.
4. Call `dto.setCapacityWarning(...)` in the three responders (`RespondWithOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, `RespondWithOwnerUpdated`) — note this helper needs the owner's city, so it takes the `owner` (or its city) plus the repository, unlike `BulkSignup`.

